{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For we have cut a covenant.</b> With death, that we shall not die now." "<b>And with Sheol we have made a vision.</b> Like a covenant. And Rabbi Moses the Kohen said: like חזוֹ (vision), by way of prophecy. But what will he do with the phrase עשינו חוזה (we have made a vision)? In my opinion, חוזה is the prophet, and likewise it is: a covenant with death, and with Sheol we have made a covenant-vision — like a covenant made through prophecy." "<b>A scourge, a sweeping scourge.</b> Concerning famine, and the nearby one [verse] that is likewise: שוט נחל שוטף (the scourge of a sweeping wadi)." "<b>For we have made.</b> The sense is: even though we have made lies our refuge. And likewise: רפאה נפשי כי חטאתי לך (Psalm 41:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {1 "The text reads חזו׳ with an abbreviation mark; resolved as חזוֹ (vision), consistent with Ibn Ezra's paraphrase of R. Moses the Kohen's interpretation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:38.024566534Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}